# purpose: CI's `policy` check on every pull request: the branch kind decides what it may change (`wsc policy`, docs/CONSUMING.md "The job pipeline"),
#          judged with the base's rules; a failure comments on the pull request.
# usage: runs on GitHub Actions; locally (after git fetch): python3 wsc.py policy --branch <branch> --base origin/main [--head <rev>]
# when: automatic on pull requests; require the "policy" check in branch protection for main.
# pull_request_target (W23, C25): GitHub runs this file as it is on main, never a pull request's copy, so a branch cannot edit its own check, and
# `wsc policy` judges the head's commits with main's code and configuration. The job has the base's privileges: no step checks out, builds,
# caches or runs the pull request's files (the policy block fetches the head as git objects; `wsc ci render` refuses a template without it).
# Draft pull requests skip it: a job's builder opens its pull request as a draft when the job reaches review, so the review sees the branch's CI
# without a `policy` that must fail until the review says merge. The reviewer marks the pull request ready BEFORE pushing the review commit
# (a skipped policy counts as passed, and `gh pr merge --auto` merges at once when the checks have passed), so the pushed head gets a real
# `policy` run; the ready_for_review run on the old head has no merge verdict and is red by design: the push cancels it, and `notify` stays silent.
name: policy
on:
  pull_request_target:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]
  # The W23 bootstrap. main's copy of this file had no pull_request_target when W23's own pull request ran, so that pull request is judged by
  # this trigger from its own copy (under decision 6 of jobs/W23/brief.md: the base predates W23). Only W23's report matches the path filter,
  # and a workflow a path filter skips reports no check, so every other pull request gets one `policy` check, from main's file. W27 removes
  # this trigger; `wsc ci render` and the `ci_render` gate warn until then.
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]
    paths: ['jobs/W23/report.md']
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: policy-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
{{wsc policy}}
{{wsc notify policy}}
